<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand of Bavaria (archbishop of Cologne)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1577">1577</a>–<a href="/years/1650">1650</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> was a Wittelsbach prince who was archbishop-elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> and prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Liège from 1612 until 1650, as well as bishop of several other sees. A leading figure of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/counter-reformation">Catholic Reformation</a>, he fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grignoux">Grignoux</a> faction in Liège and imposed his authority on the city with troops in 1649.</p></div>
